WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.131
Security detections are not one-time rules that remain useful forever.

2
00:00:04.131 --> 00:00:10.527
They depend on telemetry, environments, threat behavior, analyst workflows, and business context.

3
00:00:10.527 --> 00:00:14.777
Detection lifecycle management treats detections as living defensive assets.

4
00:00:14.777 --> 00:00:22.759
Each detection should have a purpose, owner, data source, expected behavior, documentation, review process, and improvement path.

5
00:00:22.759 --> 00:00:28.946
Without lifecycle management, detections can become noisy, outdated, duplicated, or ignored.

6
00:00:28.946 --> 00:00:34.573
A rule that once produced useful signal may lose value as systems, users, and threats change.

7
00:00:34.573 --> 00:00:42.326
The lifecycle mindset helps teams maintain a reliable portfolio of signals instead of a growing folder of unmanaged rules.
